@startuml deployment
!include style.iuml
title Recipe Builder - Deployment Diagram (AWS)

node "Cook's device" <<device>> {
  node "Web browser" <<execution environment>> {
    artifact "React app\n(HTML, JS, CSS)" as App
  }
}

cloud "Amazon Route 53" as R53 {
  artifact "Registered domain\n+ hosted zone\nA record -> Elastic IP" as Record
}

node "AWS Region" <<cloud>> {
  node "VPC" {
    node "Amazon EC2 instance" <<virtual machine>> as EC2 {
      component "Elastic IP\n(fixed public address)" as EIP
      node "Web server\n(nginx - to confirm with Jose)" <<execution environment>> as Web {
        artifact "frontend build\n(dist/)" as Dist
      }
      node "JVM (Java 17)" <<execution environment>> {
        artifact "recipe-builder.jar\n(Spring Boot)" as Jar
        artifact "/etc/recipe-builder.env\n(API key, DB password)" as Env
      }
    }
    node "Amazon RDS\n(managed PostgreSQL)" <<database server>> as RDS {
      database "recipe_builder_db\n(V1-V10, V3 skipped)" as DB
    }
  }
}

cloud "Spoonacular API\n(api.spoonacular.com)" as Spoon

App --> R53 : DNS lookup
App --> EIP : HTTPS 443 (HTTP until\nLet's Encrypt is set up)
EIP --> Web
Web --> Jar : /api proxied to :8080
Jar --> DB : JDBC :5432
Jar --> Spoon : HTTPS
Jar ..> Env : reads at startup

note bottom of EC2
  Set up by Jose: the app runs on an EC2
  virtual machine, the database on Amazon RDS,
  and the domain is registered with Route 53.
  Still to confirm: instance type, region, nginx
  vs. Spring Boot serving the frontend, HTTPS.
end note

legend right
  |= Symbol |= Meaning |
  | 3D box | a node: a machine or place where software runs |
  | node inside a node | an execution environment, e.g. the JVM on the server |
  | page icon | an artifact: a deployed file, e.g. the backend jar |
  | cylinder | a database |
  | cloud | an outside service |
  | solid arrow | a network connection, labelled with what travels over it |
  | dashed arrow | reads at startup |
endlegend
@enduml
